1
00:00:03,368 --> 00:00:09,982
February 26th, 1959 On a bare slope in the northern Urals searchers climb

2
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:15,446
toward a shape buried in wind-driven snow a large canvas tent still standing

3
00:00:15,752 --> 00:00:20,498
pitched where no experienced party would camp Its canvas has been slit open

4
00:00:20,378 --> 00:00:25,978
from the inside Boots coats and diaries are inside it The nine hikers who

5
00:00:25,661 --> 00:00:26,439
own them are gone

6
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,976
Their footprints lead downhill, toward a forest a mile and a half below.

7
00:00:33,255 --> 00:00:34,419
Some are made in socks.

8
00:00:34,712 --> 00:00:36,004
Some in single boots.

9
00:00:36,297 --> 00:00:41,069
They are spaced like people walking side by side, at an ordinary pace.

10
00:00:41,361 --> 00:00:43,530
Near the treeline, the prints stop.

11
00:00:45,598 --> 00:00:49,301
What the searchers cannot find matters as much as what they can.

12
00:00:49,593 --> 00:00:51,221
No supplies carried out.

13
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:52,097
No note.

14
00:00:52,402 --> 00:00:54,262
No trail prepared in advance.

15
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:56,607
Nothing about this exit looks planned.

16
00:00:56,900 --> 00:00:58,424
Everything about it looks sudden.

17
00:01:00,586 --> 00:01:05,732
That night, temperatures near the site fell far below minus thirty, with wind.

18
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:11,161
Nine experienced winter travelers had walked out of their only shelter, into

19
00:01:10,883 --> 00:01:12,356
the dark and the cold.

20
00:01:12,661 --> 00:01:14,160
None were seen alive again.

21
00:01:16,337 --> 00:01:21,341
For more than sixty years, investigators, scientists, and theorists have argued

22
00:01:21,376 --> 00:01:25,452
over the same question a question the case file never answers.

23
00:01:25,757 --> 00:01:26,689
Why did they leave?

24
00:01:34,968 --> 00:01:42,872
The story begins in Sverdlovsk, in January 1959 a closed industrial city five

25
00:01:42,752 --> 00:01:47,794
hundred kilometres east of Moscow At the Ural Polytechnic Institute the city's

26
00:01:47,674 --> 00:01:53,503
route commission approves a winter expedition Category III the hardest regular

27
00:01:53,383 --> 00:01:58,877
grade Sixteen days on skis north to mount Otorten Ten set out

28
00:02:01,028 --> 00:02:06,345
They are led by Igor Dyatlov, twenty-three, an engineering student who has

29
00:02:06,118 --> 00:02:08,455
run winter routes since his teens.

30
00:02:08,773 --> 00:02:13,068
With him: ski-touring partners he has trained and travelled with for years,

31
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:18,738
carrying skis, a primus stove, canvas tents, and the confidence of a group

32
00:02:18,773 --> 00:02:20,736
that has wintered in this country before.

33
00:02:21,028 --> 00:02:22,334
The youngest is twenty.

34
00:02:22,652 --> 00:02:24,499
The oldest is thirty-eight.

35
00:02:26,630 --> 00:02:32,356
The journey runs by rail to Ivdel, by truck to Vizhay the last settlement,

36
00:02:32,493 --> 00:02:37,849
where the group registers its route and then north on sledge and ski, up the

37
00:02:37,545 --> 00:02:39,018
frozen Lozva river.

38
00:02:39,310 --> 00:02:46,212
On January 28th Yuri Yudin turns back too ill to continue The farewell they

39
00:02:45,908 --> 00:02:50,487
photograph at a cart track becomes the last picture of all ten together

40
00:02:52,558 --> 00:02:58,890
On the 31st, they bury a supply cache the labaz in the bank of the Auspiya

41
00:02:58,770 --> 00:03:01,351
valley, to lighten the load for the return.

42
00:03:01,643 --> 00:03:08,107
The diaries record hard frost, and a wind that reads, entry after entry, like

43
00:03:07,803 --> 00:03:08,451
a warning.

44
00:03:08,757 --> 00:03:10,230
Ahead lies the pass.

45
00:03:10,522 --> 00:03:13,825
Beyond it, mount Otorten and nothing inhabited.

46
00:03:16,008 --> 00:03:21,814
February 1st The plan calls for crossing the 1079 pass and camping in the

47
00:03:21,459 --> 00:03:26,952
valley beyond it Instead the group drifts about a kilometre west of its line

48
00:03:27,142 --> 00:03:32,729
and in the afternoon begins climbing the open shoulder of Kholat Syakhl in

49
00:03:32,425 --> 00:03:33,512
worsening weather

50
00:03:35,551 --> 00:03:40,413
Late in the day, at about a thousand metres, they pitch the tent on the open

51
00:03:40,293 --> 00:03:45,439
slope twenty-three degrees, wind-scoured, with the forest and its shelter

52
00:03:45,319 --> 00:03:46,998
a mile and a half below.

53
00:03:47,291 --> 00:03:52,024
It is the kind of decision experienced travelers do not usually have to explain,

54
00:03:51,904 --> 00:03:53,845
because they do not usually make it.

55
00:03:54,005 --> 00:03:57,170
The last known photograph shows the tent going up.

56
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:58,893
Then the cameras go quiet.

57
00:04:00,965 --> 00:04:05,921
Everything after noon that day is reconstruction built from tracks, from the

58
00:04:05,566 --> 00:04:07,309
camp, from what was left behind.

59
00:04:07,628 --> 00:04:08,753
The diaries stop.

60
00:04:09,058 --> 00:04:10,273
The photographs stop.

61
00:04:10,566 --> 00:04:13,550
The night itself has no witness who survived it.

62
00:04:16,661 --> 00:04:21,823
February 20th with the group overdue the institute sends its first search

63
00:04:21,674 --> 00:04:28,082
parties Within days the operation grows volunteers students military aircraft

64
00:04:28,143 --> 00:04:33,653
and trackers fanning out across the valley On the 26th students climb the

65
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:39,976
slope and find the tent Inside money documents spare clothing food Everything

66
00:04:39,856 --> 00:04:43,185
a winter camp should hold except the campers

67
00:04:45,262 --> 00:04:51,352
The canvas is cut from the inside eight or nine slashes, some reachable only

68
00:04:51,203 --> 00:04:51,890
from within.

69
00:04:52,195 --> 00:04:57,344
Outside, the snow holds footprints from eight or nine people, spaced like

70
00:04:57,015 --> 00:04:59,441
a walking group, not a panicked run.

71
00:04:59,734 --> 00:05:03,372
They lead downhill toward the treeline, and there they end.

72
00:05:05,334 --> 00:05:11,090
Under a tall cedar at the forest edge a mile and a half below the tent are

73
00:05:10,785 --> 00:05:15,870
the remains of a small fire, and branches broken high up the trunk, as if

74
00:05:15,541 --> 00:05:17,645
someone had climbed for the last dry wood.

75
00:05:17,950 --> 00:05:19,076
And two bodies.

76
00:05:19,355 --> 00:05:24,166
Yuri Doroshenko and Yuri Krivonishenko, dead of exposure.

77
00:05:24,458 --> 00:05:27,220
The autopsy records burns on their hands.

78
00:05:27,512 --> 00:05:29,372
They fed that fire until they could not.

79
00:05:31,469 --> 00:05:33,909
The cedar itself carries a message.

80
00:05:34,201 --> 00:05:38,706
Its branches are broken up to five metres off the ground climbed for, in the

81
00:05:38,402 --> 00:05:41,344
dark, in lethal cold, by bare hands.

82
00:05:41,701 --> 00:05:42,289
For wood.

83
00:05:42,552 --> 00:05:45,172
Or for a view of the slope they had come down from.

84
00:05:45,477 --> 00:05:48,680
The searchers note it, and cannot explain it.

85
00:05:50,652 --> 00:05:55,643
Between the cedar and the tent, over the following days, three more are found

86
00:05:55,987 --> 00:06:00,582
spaced along the line of the footprints, several hundred metres apart, all

87
00:06:00,381 --> 00:06:01,996
facing back up the slope.

88
00:06:02,289 --> 00:06:04,664
Igor Dyatlov, near the forest.

89
00:06:04,969 --> 00:06:11,081
Then, on March 5th Rustem Slobodin and Zinaida Kolmogorova closer to the tent

90
00:06:13,103 --> 00:06:16,045
It takes the spring melt to give up the last four.

91
00:06:16,338 --> 00:06:21,075
In early May, seventy-five metres from the cedar and four metres under the

92
00:06:20,732 --> 00:06:27,115
snow, searchers find Semyon Zolotaryov, Nikolai Thibeaux-Brignolle, Lyudmila

93
00:06:27,188 --> 00:06:33,429
Dubinina, and Alexander Kolevatov beside a small den dug into the stream bank

94
00:06:33,490 --> 00:06:34,151
of a ravine.

95
00:06:36,262 --> 00:06:38,740
The autopsies divide the nine in two.

96
00:06:39,084 --> 00:06:43,006
Five died of exposure the cold alone, in every case.

97
00:06:43,285 --> 00:06:48,521
Rustem Slobodin's skull was fractured, but the pathologists ruled it non-fatal.

98
00:06:48,788 --> 00:06:51,811
Whatever broke it, they wrote, was not what stopped him.

99
00:06:53,852 --> 00:06:55,673
The last four died differently.

100
00:06:55,965 --> 00:07:00,841
Severe internal injuries one skull crushed, two chests broken in multiple

101
00:07:00,721 --> 00:07:03,830
places, the kind of force a car crash produces.

102
00:07:04,136 --> 00:07:10,518
Yet none of them carries a single external wound: no burns, no cuts, no bruises.

103
00:07:10,811 --> 00:07:13,792
The force that killed them left no mark on the skin.

104
00:07:14,084 --> 00:07:16,897
What that force was, the reports do not say.

105
00:07:19,009 --> 00:07:23,201
Two details from the file feed the legend, but they begin as facts.

106
00:07:23,494 --> 00:07:28,269
Several of the nine were found partly undressed a documented behaviour of

107
00:07:27,914 --> 00:07:29,335
terminal hypothermia.

108
00:07:29,628 --> 00:07:34,867
And a radiological appendix records beta contamination on some clothing of

109
00:07:34,525 --> 00:07:39,065
the ravine four far from lethal, origin never established.

110
00:07:41,121 --> 00:07:47,556
On May 28th the case is closed Prosecutor Lev Ivanov writes that the hikers

111
00:07:47,436 --> 00:07:52,379
died from a compelling natural force which they were unable to overcome He

112
00:07:52,010 --> 00:07:57,904
does not name the force The file is sealed the slope is quiet and the theories

113
00:07:57,784 --> 00:07:58,329
begin

114
00:08:01,586 --> 00:08:07,995
Every theory of Dyatlov Pass has to survive the same test: the evidence itself.

115
00:08:08,287 --> 00:08:10,198
Some survive better than others.

116
00:08:12,313 --> 00:08:14,804
An attack by people fails first.

117
00:08:15,097 --> 00:08:15,964
No struggle.

118
00:08:16,269 --> 00:08:17,717
No third-party tracks.

119
00:08:18,022 --> 00:08:19,882
Nothing stolen even the money.

120
00:08:20,174 --> 00:08:25,809
The Mansi, the Indigenous people of these forests, cooperated with the investigation

121
00:08:25,689 --> 00:08:30,178
from the start, and their herders moved through this country all winter without

122
00:08:30,058 --> 00:08:30,681
incident.

123
00:08:30,973 --> 00:08:34,173
The forensic record rules out violence by anyone.

124
00:08:36,308 --> 00:08:38,889
Deliberate abandonment fails next.

125
00:08:39,156 --> 00:08:43,610
No one walks out of a standing tent at minus thirty, leaves the boots, the

126
00:08:43,331 --> 00:08:46,689
coats, and the food and never comes back for them.

127
00:08:46,914 --> 00:08:52,385
The positions of the bodies say the group kept moving, and kept trying to

128
00:08:52,017 --> 00:08:52,588
live.

129
00:08:54,569 --> 00:08:57,550
The stranger theories feed on real details.

130
00:08:57,829 --> 00:09:02,872
Weeks after the search began, witnesses told investigators about glowing orange

131
00:09:02,816 --> 00:09:07,747
objects in the night sky over the northern Urals testimony that remains in

132
00:09:07,404 --> 00:09:11,390
the file, from an era of early Soviet rocket tests.

133
00:09:11,682 --> 00:09:14,625
And the contamination on the clothing is real.

134
00:09:14,930 --> 00:09:19,718
But nothing in the record places any event over the slope that night, and

135
00:09:19,376 --> 00:09:22,073
the contamination's source was never established.

136
00:09:22,353 --> 00:09:25,746
What remains is testimony and an open question.

137
00:09:27,892 --> 00:09:30,950
One more natural explanation deserves its honesty.

138
00:09:31,268 --> 00:09:37,819
Wind curling around a ridge can, in theory, produce infrasound pressure waves

139
00:09:37,699 --> 00:09:42,071
at the edge of hearing, linked in some studies to unease and dread.

140
00:09:42,364 --> 00:09:43,386
It fits the fear.

141
00:09:43,691 --> 00:09:47,084
It does not fit the injuries, the cuts, or the tracks.

142
00:09:47,389 --> 00:09:50,937
And on this slope, in this wind, it cannot be tested.

143
00:09:51,243 --> 00:09:52,870
It remains a hypothesis.

144
00:09:55,018 --> 00:09:59,880
The avalanche is the theory with the strongest forensic fit and the loudest

145
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:00,654
objections.

146
00:10:00,972 --> 00:10:06,040
The campsite slope is roughly twenty-three degrees, gentler than most avalanche

147
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:06,453
terrain.

148
00:10:06,758 --> 00:10:10,447
The searchers photographed no crown line, no debris.

149
00:10:10,753 --> 00:10:13,656
No one was buried the way an avalanche buries people.

150
00:10:13,961 --> 00:10:16,813
Twenty-six days later, the slope looked clean.

151
00:10:17,131 --> 00:10:20,499
For sixty years, that stalemate defined the case.

152
00:10:22,632 --> 00:10:28,744
Then, in January 2021 two researchers at ETH Zurich published a mechanism

153
00:10:28,805 --> 00:10:35,136
that answers every objection at once Avalanche scientist Johan Gaume and geotechnical

154
00:10:35,029 --> 00:10:36,979
engineer Alexander Puzrin

155
00:10:40,165 --> 00:10:42,837
Their model begins with the campers themselves.

156
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:48,301
To pitch the tent, the group cut a platform into the slope normal practice

157
00:10:48,193 --> 00:10:52,711
for a winter camp, and a lasting change to the layered snow above it.

158
00:10:54,648 --> 00:10:59,755
That night, strong katabatic winds behind an arctic cold front drove loose

159
00:10:59,738 --> 00:11:02,436
snow onto the shoulder above the tent.

160
00:11:02,741 --> 00:11:08,930
Hour by hour, the load built along a weak layer buried in the snowpack invisibly

161
00:11:09,081 --> 00:11:11,250
directly above the sleeping group.

162
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:18,262
The forensic window for the release: nine and a half to thirteen hours after

163
00:11:18,074 --> 00:11:19,148
the cut was made.

164
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:22,176
Sometime in the dark hours, the slab fails.

165
00:11:22,481 --> 00:11:28,555
Snow blocks up to half a cubic metre slide onto the tent a slow, heavy surf,

166
00:11:28,654 --> 00:11:30,965
moving at hardly more than walking pace.

167
00:11:31,270 --> 00:11:32,872
Pressure, not impact.

168
00:11:33,254 --> 00:11:34,470
Force without a wound.

169
00:11:36,618 --> 00:11:38,864
The model makes their escape readable too.

170
00:11:39,170 --> 00:11:44,096
A slab pressing the tent deforms the canvas, pins some of the group inside

171
00:11:44,505 --> 00:11:47,821
and the exit is cut in seconds, with knives, from within.

172
00:11:48,113 --> 00:11:53,581
Then the slope below carries them away from it: injured, freezing, alive.

173
00:11:53,925 --> 00:11:54,470
For now.

174
00:11:56,622 --> 00:12:00,763
The model's force estimates, checked against the Abbreviated Injury Scale,

175
00:12:01,158 --> 00:12:05,995
reproduce the pattern in the autopsies: moderate to severe compression injuries

176
00:12:05,875 --> 00:12:10,286
of chest and skull painful disabling, survivable.

177
00:12:10,591 --> 00:12:11,987
Everyone could still walk out.

178
00:12:12,279 --> 00:12:13,276
No one was buried.

179
00:12:15,404 --> 00:12:17,509
It also answers the objections.

180
00:12:17,814 --> 00:12:21,529
A twenty-three degree slope can release when wind adds load.

181
00:12:21,822 --> 00:12:26,916
The missing traces were erased by weeks of fresh snowfall the same smoothing

182
00:12:26,796 --> 00:12:28,720
the searchers' photographs recorded.

183
00:12:29,012 --> 00:12:34,197
In 2022 the authors came back with three expeditions and field measurements

184
00:12:34,077 --> 00:12:37,857
at the pass and found that avalanches there are not exceptional

185
00:12:39,919 --> 00:12:44,653
What the science does not do and does not claim to do is close the file.

186
00:12:44,945 --> 00:12:49,434
It does not say why no one climbed back to the tent, why the group split,

187
00:12:49,765 --> 00:12:51,508
or where the contamination came from.

188
00:12:51,788 --> 00:12:55,014
It shrinks the mystery to human-sized questions.

189
00:12:55,293 --> 00:12:57,204
That is what good evidence work does.

190
00:13:00,447 --> 00:13:04,188
Assembled, the evidence holds one defensible chain.

191
00:13:04,468 --> 00:13:05,387
A winter storm.

192
00:13:05,679 --> 00:13:06,624
A loaded slope.

193
00:13:06,916 --> 00:13:10,748
A slab released in the dark, hours after the group fell asleep.

194
00:13:11,027 --> 00:13:12,938
An exit cut in seconds.

195
00:13:13,218 --> 00:13:14,704
A descent to the trees.

196
00:13:14,983 --> 00:13:18,028
And cold finishing what fear and injury began.

197
00:13:20,170 --> 00:13:25,625
In 2020 after a re-examination requested by the families Russian prosecutors

198
00:13:25,518 --> 00:13:32,472
endorsed the same conclusion an avalanche deaths by hypothermia no crime The

199
00:13:32,103 --> 00:13:34,427
state's answer sixty-one years late

200
00:13:36,455 --> 00:13:40,325
In a sense, the 1959 closure was never wrong.

201
00:13:40,605 --> 00:13:43,946
A compelling natural force the file's own words.

202
00:13:44,265 --> 00:13:47,056
Science has spent sixty years learning how to name it.

203
00:13:49,045 --> 00:13:52,735
What remains unanswered is the part no file can close.

204
00:13:53,027 --> 00:13:57,722
The choices of nine people in the dark who decided to go down, who decided

205
00:13:57,602 --> 00:13:59,668
to go back, who stayed with whom.

206
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:03,392
The evidence shows they moved with reason and order.

207
00:14:03,684 --> 00:14:05,222
It will never show what they said.

208
00:14:07,381 --> 00:14:10,504
They were: Igor Dyatlov, twenty-three.

209
00:14:10,796 --> 00:14:13,133
Zinaida Kolmogorova, twenty.

210
00:14:13,412 --> 00:14:15,607
Rustem Slobodin, twenty-three.

211
00:14:15,912 --> 00:14:18,055
Yuri Doroshenko, twenty-one.

212
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,890
Yuri Krivonishenko, twenty-three.

213
00:14:21,183 --> 00:14:23,970
Nikolai Thibeaux-Brignolle, twenty-four.

214
00:14:24,263 --> 00:14:26,522
Lyudmila Dubinina, twenty.

215
00:14:26,827 --> 00:14:29,357
Alexander Kolevatov, twenty-five.

216
00:14:29,662 --> 00:14:32,514
And Semyon Zolotaryov, thirty-eight.

217
00:14:34,567 --> 00:14:39,958
In 1963 the pass they set out to cross was given their leader's name The slope

218
00:14:39,838 --> 00:14:44,674
still sits at twenty-three degrees The evidence still says what it has always

219
00:14:44,567 --> 00:14:49,507
said about that night and it still cannot say everything The file remains

220
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:54,880
open where the record ends with nine names one mountain and the honest limits

221
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:56,221
of what science has proven
